## 3. Non-Commercial Use

Commercial Use of the Software and Covered Works is prohibited.

The Software and Covered Works must not be:

* sold;
* rented;
* leased;
* licensed for monetary compensation;
* commercially hosted;
* commercially provided;
* monetized;
* used to obtain commercial advantage; or
* incorporated into a commercial service or product.

This prohibition applies regardless of whether the Software itself is provided without charge.

A person must not obtain commercial benefit by providing access to a Covered Work, providing Functionality of a Covered Work, or providing a service whose principal purpose is to provide access to a Covered Work.

No person may use a Covered Work as part of a paid educational institution, paid service, commercial product, commercial service, or other economically valuable offering.

---

## 4. Equal Access

Every User must receive the same Functionality under the same substantive conditions, regardless of wealth, income, ability to pay, payment status, or economic circumstances.

No Covered Work may impose an Economic Condition for access to any Functionality.

No Covered Work may provide a materially better, larger, faster, more capable, less restricted, more reliable, more convenient, or otherwise superior form of Functionality to one User because that User has paid or provided economic value.

No Covered Work may divide its Functionality into free and paid versions or otherwise reserve Functionality for paying Users.

A limitation is permitted only when it applies equally to all Users and cannot be removed, increased, reduced, bypassed, or otherwise altered through payment or economic status.

A User must not be required to pay a third party in order to receive Functionality of a Covered Work.

This requirement applies regardless of whether the payment is made to the Copyright Holder, Licensee, hosting provider, API provider, model provider, infrastructure provider, plugin developer, service operator, or any other person or entity.

A Licensee must not move a prohibited payment requirement, restriction, or superior Functionality into another component, service, account system, plugin, extension, dependency, server, or other separate work.

---

## 5. Donations

Donations are permitted only when they are entirely voluntary and provide nothing in return.

A donor must receive no:

* additional Functionality;
* additional access;
* increased capacity;
* priority;
* improved quality;
* preferential treatment;
* service;
* status;
* recognition;
* personalization;
* convenience;
* privilege; or
* other advantage.

A donor must receive nothing that a non-donor does not receive on the same terms.

A payment that provides any such benefit is not a Donation and is prohibited.

