## 10. Violation and Termination

Any violation of this License terminates the rights granted to the violating Licensee automatically upon the violation.

Upon termination, the Licensee must immediately cease exercising the rights granted by this License.

Termination removes the rights granted by this License; it does not transfer ownership of copyright or other property.

A violation by an end User does not by itself terminate the rights of an operator who did not participate in, intentionally enable, or knowingly permit the violation and who takes reasonable steps to stop the violation after becoming aware of it.

No failure by the Copyright Holder to immediately enforce a provision constitutes a waiver of that provision.

